 "note": [
  "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh). The mirror carries no Old Testament, so OT quotations reuse the wording of an already-shipped Amharic work where one quotes the same verse (source_file names it) and are otherwise self_rendered in the 1962 register. The English edition quotes the KJV; where the 1962 text differs (e.g. Galatians 2:20 'faith in', Ephesians 5:21 'fear of Christ', Romans 8:1 without the KJV's closing clause, Mark 9:24 without 'with tears') the 1962 wording was kept verbatim.",
  "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: an exact substring of at least 20 characters of the 1962 NT verse (or 25 of the cited corpus file) inside that block. Shorter, re-personed or uncited-allusion quotations are self_rendered, whatever the translator believed. The mirror bridges some verse ranges into one entry holding only partial text (e.g. Ephesians 1:18-22, 1 Thessalonians 5:20-22, Luke 4:9-12, John 14:15-17), so verses inside those ranges were not quoted from it."
 ],
